# Ship after every commit

A post-commit hook pushes the current branch to `origin`. On `main`, with a clean worktree, it deploys production with `vercel deploy --prod --yes`.

When a prompt changes project files:

1. Commit the change. Leave secrets out (`.env*`, credentials, `.vercel`).
2. Read the hook output. If the push or the production deploy did not finish, do that step yourself.
3. Skip the commit when there is nothing new to commit.

Never force-push and never skip hooks.
